Note, Word Predictor Training.

Note, Global state.
Let vocab size be 0.
Let trained be no.
Let epoch loss be 0.
Let total epochs be 0.
Create a list called words.
Create a list called idx to word.
Create a dictionary called word to idx.
Create a list called weights.
Let training text be none.

Note, Build vocabulary from the words list.
Define build vocab,
    Set vocab size to 0.
    Create a list called new idx to word.
    Create a dictionary called new word to idx.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to the length of words,
        Let w be item wi of words.
        If not the value of new word to idx has the entry the value of w,
            Add 1 to vocab size.
            Add w to new idx to word.
            Set the entry the value of w in new word to idx to the value of vocab size.
        End if.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Set idx to word to the value of new idx to word.
    Set word to idx to the value of new word to idx.
End define.

Note, Initialize weights with small random values.
Define init weights,
    Create a list called new weights.
    Let total be the value of vocab size times vocab size.
    Let wi be 0.
    While the value of wi is less than total,
        Let w be a random decimal between negative 0 point 1 and 0 point 1.
        Add w to new weights.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Set weights to the value of new weights.
End define.

Note, Train one epoch and return average loss.
Define train one epoch that takes lr,
    Let total loss be 0.
    Let pair count be 0.
    Let ti be 1.
    Let num words be the length of words.
    While the value of ti is less than num words,
        Let current word be item ti of words.
        Let next ti be the value of ti plus 1.
        Let target word be item next ti of words.
        Let from idx be the entry the value of current word in word to idx.
        Let to idx be the entry the value of target word in word to idx.

        Note, Forward pass, extract logits row.
        Create a list called logits.
        Let row offset be the value of from idx minus 1 times vocab size.
        Let ki be 1.
        While the value of ki is less than or equal to vocab size,
            Let widx be the value of row offset plus ki.
            Let logit be item widx of weights.
            Add logit to logits.
            Add 1 to ki.
        End while.

        Note, Softmax with numerical stability.
        Let max logit be the max of logits.
        Create a list called probs.
        Let exp total be 0.
        Let ki be 1.
        While the value of ki is less than or equal to vocab size,
            Let logit be item ki of logits.
            Let shifted be the value of logit minus max logit.
            Let ex be the exponential of shifted.
            Add ex to probs.
            Set exp total to the value of exp total plus ex.
            Add 1 to ki.
        End while.
        Let ki be 1.
        While the value of ki is less than or equal to vocab size,
            Let p be item ki of probs.
            Set item ki of probs to the value of p divided by exp total.
            Add 1 to ki.
        End while.

        Note, Cross entropy loss.
        Let target prob be item to idx of probs.
        If the value of target prob is less than 0 point 0000001,
            Set target prob to 0 point 0000001.
        End if.
        Let loss be the logarithm of the value of target prob.
        Set loss to the value of loss times negative 1.
        Set total loss to the value of total loss plus loss.
        Add 1 to pair count.

        Note, Backward pass, update weights for this row.
        Let ki be 1.
        While the value of ki is less than or equal to vocab size,
            Let grad be item ki of probs.
            If the value of ki is equal to to idx,
                Set grad to the value of grad minus 1.
            End if.
            Let widx be the value of row offset plus ki.
            Let old w be item widx of weights.
            Let step be the value of grad times lr.
            Set item widx of weights to the value of old w minus step.
            Add 1 to ki.
        End while.

        Add 1 to ti.
    End while.

    If the value of pair count is greater than 0,
        Set epoch loss to the value of total loss divided by pair count.
    End if.
    Return the value of epoch loss.
End define.

Note, Save model to database.
Define handle save,
    Open a database called word predictor.
    Create a table called vocab with columns word and idx.
    Let vi be 1.
    While the value of vi is less than or equal to vocab size,
        Let w be item vi of idx to word.
        Insert into vocab the values the value of w and the value of vi.
        Add 1 to vi.
    End while.
    Create a table called weights with columns pos and val.
    Let total be the value of vocab size times vocab size.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to total,
        Let w be item wi of weights.
        Insert into weights the values the value of wi and the value of w.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Create a table called config with columns key and val.
    Insert into config the values vocabsize and the value of vocab size.
    Insert into config the values epochs and the value of total epochs.
    Close the database.
    Set trained to yes.
    Say Model saved to database.
    Call show ui.
End define.

Note, Load training text from file.
Define handle load file,
    Let filepath be the text box filepath.
    Read the file the value of filepath and store it in content.
    Set training text to the value of content.
    Say File loaded.
    Call show ui.
End define.

Note, Start training.
Define handle train,
    Let raw epochs be the text box epochs.
    Let raw lr be the text box lr.
    Let num epochs be the number of raw epochs.
    Let lr be the number of raw lr.
    Let raw text be the text box traintext.
    Let raw len be the length of raw text.
    If the value of raw len is greater than 0,
        Set training text to the value of raw text.
    End if.
    If the value of training text is equal to none,
        Say Please enter training text or load a file.
        Return 0.
    End if.
    Set words to the split of training text by space.
    Call build vocab.
    Call init weights.
    Say Training with the value of vocab size joined with words.
    Let epoch be 1.
    While the value of epoch is less than or equal to num epochs,
        Call train one epoch with the value of lr and store the result in loss.
        Set total epochs to the value of epoch.
        Clear window.
        Add label Training in progress.
        Add label Epoch the value of epoch of the value of num epochs.
        Add label Loss the value of epoch loss.
        Add label Vocab the value of vocab size joined with words.
        Add button with text Save Model that calls handle save.
        Add button with text Train Again that calls show ui.
        Add 1 to epoch.
    End while.
    Say Training done.
    Say the value of epoch loss.
End define.

Note, Main UI.
Define show ui,
    Clear window.
    Add label Word Predictor Training.
    Add label Enter text or load from file.
    Add text box traintext.
    Add label File path.
    Add text box filepath.
    Add button with text Load File that calls handle load file.
    Add label Epochs and learning rate.
    Add text box epochs.
    Add text box lr.
    Add button with text Start Training that calls handle train.
    If the value of trained is equal to yes,
        Add label Model saved.
    End if.
End define.

Note, Launch window.
Open window with title Word Predictor Training.
Set window size to 500 by 600.
Set background color to #1e1e2e.
Set text color to #cdd6f4.
Set font size to 13.
Call show ui.
Wait for close.
